<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every user-visible string in the Editor Workspace.

  Kept here rather than inline so the wording of a load-bearing message (the
  stale-source warning, the destructive reset confirmation, a rejection reason)
  can be reviewed in one place instead of hunted through view code.

  ONE VOCABULARY FOR THE CONSTRUCTION/SCULPT SEAM. Nothing the user reads says
  "Freeze" or "frozen". Those name the implementation's act — copying the
  Construction mesh into an editable sculpt mesh — and the user's act is
  "start sculpting". The reversible semantics are unchanged and the copy says so:
  the Construction Source is kept, Back to Construction returns to it, Resume
  Sculpt comes back to the same mesh, and Reset Sculpt from Shape is still the
  one destructive act and is still confirmed. Internal names below JNI, the view
  ids and the architecture's own terms keep "freeze", because they are accurate
  about what the code does and renaming them would be churn with no reader.
-->
<resources>
