    <!--
      The primary Construction → Sculpt action. It is what the USER does; the
      mesh copy the product makes to allow it is not the user's business and is
      not named here. The act is still reversible in exactly the way it was:
      the Construction Source is kept and Back to Construction returns to it.
    -->
    <string name="start_sculpting">Start Sculpting</string>
    <string name="resume_sculpt">Resume Sculpt</string>
    <string name="back_to_construction">Back to Construction</string>
    <!--
      The same act on a row too narrow to carry the full wording, and the ONLY
      abbreviated label in the product.

      Back to Construction is the one way out of Sculpt Mode, so it may not be
      truncated to "Back to Constructi…" — a critical destination the user has to
      guess at is not navigation. Where the row genuinely cannot carry the
      sentence, it carries the destination plus the direction instead, which is
      unambiguous on its own. It is never announced: the content description
      stays the full wording in both forms, so nothing changes for a screen
      reader with the window size. See GlobalToolbarView#applyTransitionLabel.
    -->
    <string name="back_to_construction_short">← Construction</string>

    <!--
      The same act for a body whose geometry came from a file (IMPORT-01B).

      A different word because it is a different destination and the user can
      see which: an Imported Mesh has no Construction shape behind it, and
      "Back to Construction" over one would name a place that does not exist.
      What the code does is identical — it leaves Sculpt mode and republishes
      the body's SOURCE representation — and the source is just as untouched.
    -->
    <string name="back_to_imported_mesh">Back to Imported Mesh</string>
    <!--
      Its abbreviated form, on the same terms as back_to_construction_short and
      for the same reason: this is the one way out of Sculpt Mode and may not be
      truncated to a guess. The content description stays the full wording.
    -->
    <string name="back_to_imported_mesh_short">← Imported Mesh</string>
    <!--
      The editing context an Imported Mesh is in when it is not being sculpted.

      "Construction" was drawn there until IMPORT-01B, which was already a
      little wrong — an imported body has no Construction Source — and became
      plainly wrong once the way back out of Sculpt started naming the Imported
      Mesh. The label says which representation the user is looking at; the
      mode-independent behaviour around it is unchanged.
    -->
    <string name="context_imported_mesh">Imported Mesh</string>
    <!--
      Export. `export` is the DRAWN label, unchanged from when the control was
